id: pm-mcxk8v
title: "GH-1028: history-author-acknowledge bulk mutation lacks dry-run and misreports empty selection"
description: "The irreversible history-author-acknowledge --all-actionable path can mutate every actionable item-id:line coordinate without a preview plan. When the selector matches zero actionable coordinates it emits a misleading validation-style diagnostic instead of the effect-aware no_effect result, making recovery unsafe to plan and hard to automate."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[8]: agent-ux,author-attribution,bulk-mutation,destructive-safety,dry-run,github-1028,history,zero-selection
created_at: "2026-08-15T10:38:43.585Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-15T16:32:08.269Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-15T16:20:46.304Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-15T16:20:46.304Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Add one SDK-native selector/plan primitive used by CLI and MCP; preserve the existing exclusive selector grammar of repeated --event item-id:line coordinates or --all-actionable; expose --dry-run and return selection.kind, deterministic item_id then line ordering, selected_count, omitted_count, bounded coordinates, and a stable plan_fingerprint computed over the complete ordered coordinate set plus source event hashes; require apply to provide CLI --plan-fingerprint, SDK planFingerprint, or MCP plan_fingerprint and reject any re-resolved fingerprint mismatch with CONFLICT exit 4 before mutation; use the existing effect-aware exits with zero matches or an all-already-acknowledged selection returning outcome no_effect and exit 6, a mixed actionable/already-acknowledged explicit selection returning partial_effect and exit 7, malformed selectors returning USAGE exit 2, and tracker/history corruption returning GENERIC_FAILURE exit 1; keep CLI, SDK action, MCP, contracts, completions, docs, and tests in parity; add unit, integration, acceptance, selection-drift, and disposable-directory manual proof."
goal: project management = context management
objective: "Make immutable author-attribution recovery previewable, explicit, and automation-safe for both non-empty and empty selections."
value: Agents can plan a destructive recovery from CLI output without inspecting implementation code or risking an irreversible bulk mutation.
impact: "Operators can acknowledge the wrong attribution set at workspace scale, while automation cannot distinguish a healthy empty selection from a validation failure."
outcome: "CLI, SDK action, contracts, MCP exposure, completions, docs, and tests share one preview/apply/zero-selection contract for history-author-acknowledge."
why_now: The new GitHub report exposes a safety hole in an immutable-history maintenance command; it must be modeled before any further bulk-recovery UX is consolidated.
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: "pm CLI history-author-acknowledge command, current main at 996313a99bf7df942111cac40b8ada53107dcfe5; GitHub issue #1028 report"
repro_steps: Run history-author-acknowledge with --all-actionable in a disposable tracker containing actionable unknown-author coordinates; observe that no dry-run/plan exists before immutable acknowledgement. Repeat where the selector yields zero actionable coordinates and inspect the diagnostic and exit behavior.
resolution: "Fixed by an SDK-native source-hashed acknowledgment planner whose exact fingerprint is required for apply, with deterministic bounded preview and effect-aware outcomes."
expected_result: "Bulk acknowledgement first returns a deterministic preview plan over item-id:line coordinates or all_actionable. Apply consumes that exact plan fingerprint and rejects selection drift. Zero actionable coordinates produce the standard no_effect outcome rather than a validation failure."
actual_result: "The command jumps directly from selection to irreversible acknowledgement, and an empty selection is diagnosed as though the tracker or input were invalid rather than reporting that no coordinates matched."
